# MeritOS / AI LISTER — backend environment template
#
# Copy this file to backend/.env (or export these vars in your shell)
# before starting the backend. Nothing here is required for the app
# to boot — every value is optional. Missing values simply mean the
# corresponding feature reports an honest "not configured" state in
# the Settings / Sources UI. The frontend NEVER reads these values;
# only the backend does, and secrets are never echoed back to the UI.
#
# Ports (dev): backend 8421, frontend 5421. Vite proxy is already
# configured to talk to http://127.0.0.1:8421 — see frontend/vite.config.ts.
# Do not change BACKEND_PORT without also changing the Vite proxy target.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime ports
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# BACKEND_PORT=8421
# FRONTEND_PORT=5421

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional AI provider (Settings → AI provider also stores these in
# backend/data/config.json at runtime; env wins when both are set)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# AILISTER_AI_PROVIDER=            # none | openai_compatible | groq | gemini | local | mock
# AILISTER_AI_BASE_URL=
# AILISTER_AI_MODEL=
# AILISTER_AI_KEY=
# AILISTER_LOCAL_KEY=               # only for provider=local (rarely needed)

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gmail connector (OAuth 2.0 + PKCE; gmail.readonly intake + gmail.send for
# candidate emails you explicitly approve and confirm — never automatic)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two naming conventions are accepted, and the first non-empty one
# wins. Use whichever matches your Google Cloud Console copy/paste:
#
#   Preferred (project convention, matches AILISTER_AI_* prefix):
# AILISTER_GMAIL_CLIENT_ID=
# AILISTER_GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=
# AILISTER_GMAIL_REDIRECT_URI=http://127.0.0.1:8421/api/sources/gmail/oauth/callback
#
#   Alias (matches the env-var names shown in the Sources UI hint
#   and the Google OAuth docs):
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://127.0.0.1:8421/api/sources/gmail/oauth/callback
#
# Setup in Google Cloud Console:
#   1. Create an OAuth client (type: Web application).
#   2. Enable the Gmail API for the project.
#   3. Add the redirect URI above verbatim under
#      "Authorized redirect URIs".
#   4. Paste the client ID + secret into backend/.env (or into the
#      Gmail card on the Sources page — it saves them to the local
#      config file instead).
#   5. Restart the backend, open Sources, click "Connect Gmail".
#
# If neither pair is provided, the Sources page shows:
#   "Gmail OAuth is not configured"
# and the Gmail card stays in setup-required state — the app never
# fakes a connected status.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project stability lock (temporary 28-day policy, expires 2026-11-05)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repository identity validation is always active and cannot be disabled.
# The temporary lock below can be extended or removed explicitly:
#   MERITOS_PROJECT_STABILITY_LOCK=false   # remove the temporary policy
#   MERITOS_STABILITY_LOCK_EXPIRES_AT=YYYY-MM-DD  # extend the policy
# MERITOS_PROJECT_STABILITY_LOCK=true
# MERITOS_STABILITY_LOCK_EXPIRES_AT=2026-11-05
